# requirements/testing/quality.ears
capability: Testing and quality gates
owner: harness
requirements:
  - id: TST-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The harness shall fail CI when an approved requirement with verification test has no passing test marker."
    rationale: "Requirements become a checkable artifact (ADR-005)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/coverage-gate.test.ts::[TST-001] counts failing and skipped tests as not covering"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/coverage-gate.test.ts::[TST-001] fails a marker that names no requirement"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/coverage-gate.test.ts::[TST-001] fails an approved test requirement with no passing marker"
  - id: TST-002
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a change adds a use case, port, adapter or gate without an .ears change, then the harness shall fail CI."
    rationale: "Behaviour without a requirement is unreviewable."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/guard.test.ts::[TST-002] fails a new use case without an .ears change"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/guard.test.ts::[TST-002] ignores edits, deletions and package markers"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/guard.test.ts::[TST-002] passes the same change when an .ears file changes too"
  - id: TST-003
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The test suite shall run one contract suite per driven port against its fake and each available real adapter."
    rationale: "Fakes must never pass what real adapters fail (ADR-006)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T5]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestArtifactStore::test_get_returns_exactly_what_was_put"
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestLedger::test_append_returns_a_signed_chained_entry"
      - "python/tests.contract.test_kernel_fakes.TestUnitOfWork::test_state_and_events_commit_together"
      - "python/tests.integration.test_real_adapters.TestCpuExecutor::test_runs_every_task_and_checkpoints_each"
      - "python/tests.integration.test_real_adapters.TestGitSignedLedger::test_append_returns_a_signed_chained_entry"
      - "python/tests.integration.test_real_adapters.TestNasArtifactStore::test_get_returns_exactly_what_was_put"
      - "python/tests.integration.test_real_adapters.TestPostgresDatasetRepository::test_registered_raw_metadata_cannot_be_rewritten"
      - "python/tests.integration.test_real_adapters.TestPostgresUnitOfWork::test_state_and_events_commit_together"
  - id: TST-004
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The harness shall fail the mutation ratchet when a package's score drops more than 2 points below its high-water mark."
    rationale: "Test strength may not silently erode."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T10]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/ratchet.test.ts::[TST-004] allows a drop of up to 2 points below the high-water mark"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/ratchet.test.ts::[TST-004] fails a drop of more than 2 points"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/ratchet.test.ts::[TST-004] fails when a tracked package has no score"
  - id: TST-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The architecture tests shall reject mocks under domain, application or science modules."
    rationale: "Mock-heavy tests pass while adapters fail (ADR-006)."
    verification: analysis
    tiers: [lint]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.architecture.test_architecture::test_no_mocks_or_pickle_in_kernel_or_fakes"
  - id: TST-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The release report shall claim only reproducibility levels whose tiers passed in that run."
    rationale: "A reproducibility claim must be backed by the tier that proves it."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/report.test.ts::[TST-006] a failing test fails its tier even if others passed"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/report.test.ts::[TST-006] grants Level 1 when T9 passed and refuses Level 2 without T7 and T8"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/report.test.ts::[TST-006] never grants Level 4 without cited independent evidence"
  - id: TST-007
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If the harness's re-derived verdict differs from the kernel's, then the harness shall block publication."
    rationale: "The verdict is computed twice, independently."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T7, harness]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/rederive-verdict.test.ts::[TST-007] agrees with the kernel on its candidate manifest"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/rederive-verdict.test.ts::[TST-007] agrees with the kernel on its rejected manifest"
      - "typescript/packages/spec-harness/test/rederive-verdict.test.ts::[TST-007] agrees with the kernel on its verified manifest"
  - id: TST-008
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The harness shall reject a requirement whose text does not state exactly one obligation of a named system in an EARS pattern without vague wording."
    rationale: "A requirement with two obligations, no subject or a word like 'appropriate' cannot be verified by one test (INCOSE GtWR; ESI.ts spec:audit)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
  - id: TST-009
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The mutation tool shall fail unless its known-weak fixture shows at least one killed and one surviving mutant."
    rationale: "A mutation run that cannot go red, or cannot show a weak test, manufactures confidence (ESI.ts known-weak fixture)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
  - id: TST-010
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The harness shall reject a Gherkin Rule that is not titled with the id and exact text of a live requirement or that has no scenario."
    rationale: "A Rule is the executable form of a requirement; it may neither drift from the .ears text nor stand without a scenario."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
